Parent: 1415

## Context
Skill descriptions are listed in every session of every project: 38 harness
skills plus arena, 6282 description chars (measured 2026-11-01). The author's
option: make the harness doctors and arena project-specific. Candidates:
harness-doctor ("harness only", 121), arena (lives in ~/CNRS/code/arena, feeds
the harness route grid, 86), trace-doctor (surveys all sessions but runs from
the harness, 158; author's call). test-doctor stays global: coding-python.md
and workflow.md send any project to it. rules/workflow.md points to
skills/harness-doctor/references/diagnosis-discipline.md by path; that file
must stay readable from any project.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The scoped skills are listed only in their project on Claude Code, Codex and Pi (project_skill_roots in adapters/pilot-support.json), and the installer stops projecting them globally
- [ ] Pointers to their files from global rules and skills still resolve
- [ ] Measured catalog saving recorded in the PR

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise holds: no project scoping yet beyond `project_skill_roots` in adapters/pilot-support.json. Author ruling on the ticket adds trace-doctor to harness-doctor and arena.
- Simplest path: drive scoping from the existing `project_skill_roots` data; the installer skips those skills when projecting globally. test-doctor stays global.
- Check: rules/workflow.md's pointer to skills/harness-doctor/references/diagnosis-discipline.md is a repo path, so it resolves only from the harness; confirm how other projects read it today (installed absolute path?) and keep that reachable.
- Shares the installer with 1413 (wave 2).
